---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', url: '/privacy/' }]} title="Privacy Policy | MSDEVBUILD Azure" description="How MSDEVBUILD Azure handles your data: progress stays in your browser, Google sign-in is optional for sync, and usage is counted anonymously without cookies." wide={false}>
  <div class="lesson">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: 20 November 2026</em></p>
    <p>The short version: you can use everything on this site without an account. If you sign in, we keep a copy of your study progress so it follows you between devices. We count how the site is used, but never who uses it.</p>

    <h2 id="what">What stays on your device</h2>
    <p>Your learning progress (completed lessons, quiz and mock exam scores, XP, streaks, badges, your practice deck, study plan and practice certificate), plus settings like theme and currency, are stored in your browser's <code>localStorage</code>. An unfinished mock exam is kept in <code>sessionStorage</code> so a refresh doesn't lose it. If you don't sign in, none of this is sent to us.</p>

    <h2 id="accounts">Signing in (optional)</h2>
    <p>You can sign in with Google to sync your progress across devices. Sign-in is handled by Google Firebase Authentication. We receive your name, email address, profile picture and a user ID from Google. We don't receive your password.</p>
    <p>While you're signed in, the progress listed above is copied to a private record in Google Cloud Firestore that only your account can read or write. We use it only to sync your progress. We don't email you, share it or sell it.</p>

    <h2 id="discussion">Course discussion (Giscus and GitHub)</h2>
    <p>The discussion on each course page (for example <a href="/az-900/#discussion">AZ-900</a>) runs on <a href="https://giscus.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Giscus ↗</a>, which keeps comments in GitHub Discussions. It loads only when you scroll to it. Reading needs no account. To post, reply or react you sign in with GitHub inside the widget. Your comments are public on GitHub under your GitHub name, and GitHub's and Giscus's privacy policies apply (<a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a>, <a href="https://github.com/giscus/giscus/blob/main/PRIVACY-POLICY.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Giscus ↗</a>). We don't store comments ourselves.</p>

    <h2 id="counts">Anonymous usage counts</h2>
    <p>To understand how the site is used, we count events: a visit (once per browser per day), a new learner (once per browser), a lesson completed, a quiz taken, a mock exam sat, a lab finished and a new sign-in. Each event only adds 1 to a daily total. There are no cookies, no IDs, and nothing that links a count to you.</p>
    <p>We don't count anything if your browser sends a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal. We don't use Google Analytics. The ads described below are the only advertising on the site.</p>

    <h2 id="ads">Google AdSense and cookies</h2>
    <p>[EDIT] To keep every lesson, lab and mock exam free, some pages show ads served by Google AdSense. Google and its partners may use cookies or similar technology to show ads based on your visits to this and other websites. You can turn off personalised ads in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Ad Settings ↗</a>, and read how Google uses data in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites that use its services ↗</a>.</p>
    <p>[EDIT] Visitors in the European Economic Area, the UK and Switzerland see a consent message from Google before any ad cookies are set, and can change their choice at any time from the "Privacy and cookie settings" link that Google adds to the page.</p>
    <p>[EDIT] There are no ads on simulations, labs, the mock exam, interview practice, flashcards, My Progress, the certificate page or these legal pages. Supporters see no ads at all. Ads never appear while you're offline.</p>
    <p>[EDIT] Some recommended resources are affiliate links, marked "Affiliate link". If you buy through one, the site may earn a small commission at no cost to you. Sponsors of a learning track are shown with a "Sponsor" label.</p>

    <h2 id="third-party">Third parties</h2>
    <p>The site is served as static files from GitHub Pages. Sign-in, sync and counts use Google Firebase, which processes data under <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Firebase privacy terms ↗</a>. Ads are served by Google AdSense under the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy ↗</a>. Links to Microsoft Learn and other sites are governed by those sites' own privacy policies.</p>

    <h2 id="control">Your control</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>On this device:</strong> erase everything with “Reset my progress” on the <a href="/progress/">My Progress</a> page, or by clearing this site's data in your browser.</li>
      <li><strong>Synced copy:</strong> when signed in, use “Delete my synced data” on the My Progress page. It removes your cloud record straight away. Signing out keeps your progress on the device you're using.</li>
      <li><strong>Comments:</strong> edit or delete your own comment from the menu on it in the course discussion, or on GitHub.</li>
      <li><strong>Questions:</strong> <a href="https://blog.msdevbuild.com/contact/">contact us</a> and we'll help.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
